WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:16.400
students and teachers.

2
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.463
Because of heavy snow, we will close the school at two o'clock today," Ms.

3
00:00:21.503 --> 00:00:23.904
Folani's voice announced over the loudspeaker.

4
00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:27.166
"We want everyone to get home safely."

5
00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:33.249
In her second-grade room, Nina wondered, "Will we have Kids Central today?"

6
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:37.492
In his third-grade room, Jason wondered the same thing.

7
00:00:38.793 --> 00:00:41.555
Just then Miss Shelly stuck her head in the door.

8
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:44.797
"We'll start Kids Central at two today.

9
00:00:45.658 --> 00:00:48.320
You'll stay until your parents arrive to pick you up, okay?"

10
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.220
she said.

11
00:00:50.201 --> 00:00:51.081
Jason nodded.

12
00:00:51.502 --> 00:00:53.243
Bobby gave her a thumbs-up sign.

13
00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:57.846
"Nina, Izzie, and Bobby, your moms just called.

14
00:00:58.747 --> 00:01:01.728
They will be here at four o'clock," Miss Shelly said.

15
00:01:01.748 --> 00:01:05.330
"That gives us just enough time for our activity.

16
00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.531
Did you all bring your aprons?"

17
00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:10.012
"What about my dad?"

18
00:01:10.392 --> 00:01:11.212
Jason asked.

19
00:01:11.232 --> 00:01:13.213
"When is he coming?"

20
00:01:14.494 --> 00:01:17.315
Jason's dad always picked him up on Wednesdays.

21
00:01:18.315 --> 00:01:20.656
And they always went out for pizza afterward.

22
00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:25.078
"I haven't gotten a call from your dad yet.

23
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:30.668
But don't worry, I'm sure he'll come at five o'clock as usual," Miss Shelly said.

24
00:01:30.688 --> 00:01:36.110
"Today we'll bake snow brownies," said Miss Shelly.

25
00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.491
"Yay! Brownies," Izzie said.

26
00:01:40.511 --> 00:01:43.872
"But what's a snow brownie?"

27
00:01:45.312 --> 00:01:47.273
Jason didn't hear Miss Shelly's answer.

28
00:01:48.213 --> 00:01:49.973
He was still thinking about his dad.

29
00:01:51.394 --> 00:01:52.514
Why hadn't he called?

30
00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:57.656
"Step 1: Preheat the oven to 175 degrees Celsius.

31
00:02:01.108 --> 00:02:02.609
Jason, would you do that?"

32
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:03.890
Miss Shelly asked.

33
00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:06.873
"What? Oh, okay."

34
00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:09.655
Jason set the temperature on the oven.

35
00:02:11.657 --> 00:02:14.459
"Step 2: Grease a baking pan.

36
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.742
Miss Shelly, can I grease the pan this time?"

37
00:02:19.163 --> 00:02:19.923
Nina asked.

38
00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:21.805
"Of course.

39
00:02:22.465 --> 00:02:25.748
Here is some oil and a paper towel," the teacher said.

40
00:02:32.276 --> 00:02:33.677
"Who will read step 3?"

41
00:02:33.697 --> 00:02:39.401
"Me! Step 3: Beat the melted butter and sugar.

42
00:02:39.921 --> 00:02:40.762
Sugar, please."

43
00:02:41.622 --> 00:02:43.464
Izzie held out her hand for the sugar.

44
00:02:49.207 --> 00:02:51.269
"Step 4," Bobby read.

45
00:02:51.289 --> 00:03:05.065
"Beat in eggs and "Step 5: Stir in cocoa powder and flour.

46
00:03:08.506 --> 00:03:10.266
Hellooo, Jason!

47
00:03:10.886 --> 00:03:12.127
Can you pour the flour?"

48
00:03:12.147 --> 00:03:13.487
Nina asked.

49
00:03:13.507 --> 00:03:17.848
"Step 6: Stir in salt and baking powder."

50
00:03:19.289 --> 00:03:21.409
Izzie added the salt and baking powder.

51
00:03:26.271 --> 00:03:27.191
ready to bake!"

52
00:03:28.151 --> 00:03:30.372
Miss Shelly lifted the pan into the oven.

53
00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.702
"These should be done in about 27 minutes."

54
00:03:36.442 --> 00:03:40.885
While the brownies baked, the kids measured the snow that had collected on the windows.

55
00:03:40.905 --> 00:03:43.106
"12 centimeters here!"

56
00:03:43.406 --> 00:03:44.147
Izzie cried.

57
00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.752
to turn these into snow brownies," Miss Shelly called.

58
00:03:53.572 --> 00:03:56.794
Each kid placed a paper snowflake over the baking pan.

59
00:03:57.395 --> 00:03:59.536
Miss Shelly shook powdered sugar on top.

60
00:04:01.108 --> 00:04:05.252
When the kids lifted the paper snowflakes, there was a pretty snow pattern.

61
00:04:06.553 --> 00:04:08.014
Five o'clock came and went.

62
00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:13.799
After everyone left, Miss Shelly and Jason cleaned the tables and washed the dishes.

63
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.701
Then they read a book together.

64
00:04:17.862 --> 00:04:21.005
Finally, at six o'clock, the gym door opened.

65
00:04:21.025 --> 00:04:25.709
"What is that delicious smell?"

66
00:04:26.149 --> 00:04:26.930
a man asked.

67
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:31.771
"Dad!" Jason jumped up and ran to his father.

68
00:04:32.992 --> 00:04:33.893
"Sorry I'm late.

69
00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:38.699
I was in a meeting and couldn't use my phone," his dad said.

70
00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:40.701
"Ready to go home?

71
00:04:41.702 --> 00:04:43.925
I'm afraid it's too snowy for pizza."

72
00:04:43.945 --> 00:04:45.627
"That's okay.

73
00:04:46.628 --> 00:04:48.150
We can have brownies for dinner!"

74
00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.351
Jason said.
